{#
  chat/wing-left.njk — the welcome wing, included BEFORE the player.

  Left and right are separate files precisely because they go on opposite
  sides of the video: one include emitting both would put them side by side
  and leave the film pushed off to one end of the row.

  The author's wording. This is what a newcomer arriving mid-evening reads
  first, so it greets them and says who is hosting and where they are before
  it says anything about the film. "Welcome to" sits above the chat's name as
  a quiet italic lead-in, so the two read as one sentence while the name keeps
  the weight of a title. The gold picks out what a newcomer would look for.

  Lines that give way on a short wing carry a class saying so (see the
  chatwelcome container queries in chat-session.css) rather than being picked
  by position, so reordering a line cannot hide the wrong one.
  The <wbr> lets the website break at its dot on a narrow wing, never
  inside the word.
#}
<aside class="chat-wing chat-wing--left" aria-label="Welcome">
    <div class="chat-welcome">
        <p class="chat-welcome-lead"><span class="chat-welcome-greet">Welcome to</span> <span class="chat-welcome-name">Words of Plainness Chat</span></p>
        <p class="chat-welcome-line chat-welcome-line--mid"><span class="chat-welcome-gold">Christ-Centered</span> Ministry and Fellowship</p>
        <p class="chat-welcome-line">Host: <span class="chat-welcome-gold">Brother Aaron</span></p>
        <p class="chat-welcome-line chat-welcome-line--mid">Website: <span class="chat-welcome-gold">wordsofplainness.<wbr>org</span></p>
        <p class="chat-welcome-line chat-welcome-line--close chat-welcome-gap">I appreciate constructive feedback.</p>
        <p class="chat-welcome-line chat-welcome-line--close">May God bless us with His Spirit.</p>
    </div>
</aside>
